    {
      "id": "a1-u01-d03-t01",
      "before": "a1-u01-d03-e02",
      "title": { "en": "ę and ą" },
      "body": { "en": "Ę and ą are nasal vowels, said partly through the nose. Ę is close to \"en\" and ą to \"on\", as in French \"bon\": dziękuję, w porządku. At the very end of a word ę is said almost like a plain e, so proszę ends in \"sheh\". Ą never starts a word." }
    },
    {
      "id": "a1-u01-d03-t02",
      "before": "a1-u01-d03-e06",
      "title": { "en": "Thank you and you're welcome" },
      "body": { "en": "Dziękuję is thank you, and dzięki is thanks, said among friends. The usual replies are proszę and nie ma za co. Bardzo means very, and can come before or after: dziękuję bardzo, bardzo dziękuję." }
    }
  ],
